


- Results:

  The MLFQ xv6 kernel was tested with both single-CPU (CPUS=1) and multi-CPU (CPUS=3)
  configurations. In all cases, the system booted successfully and remained stable under
  normal and heavy workloads. The implemented getpinfo system call and the ps 
  program correctly reported process information, including priority levels. The
  MLFQ scheduler exhibited the expected behavior. Newly created processes 
  started at the highest priority level, CPU-intensive processes were gradually
  demoted to lower priority queues, and interactive processes retained higher priority.
  Starvation was avoided through priority boosting, and round-robin scheduling was applied
  within each priority level. Finally, the kernel passed the complete usertests suite,
  concluding with ALL TESTS PASSED, confirming the implementation.



